Ours.  bdfReadFont left info.defaultCh as the caller had it when the BDF has no
DEFAULT_CHAR property; bdftopcf's FontRec is on its stack, so such fonts got a
stack byte as their default character, and two builds differed.  It starts at
NO_SUCH_CHAR, as the PCF readers expect for "none".

--- a/lib/font/bitmap/bdfread.c
+++ b/lib/font/bitmap/bdfread.c
@@ -798,6 +798,10 @@
     bitmapFont->bitmapExtra->glyphNames = 0;
     bitmapFont->bitmapExtra->sWidths = 0;
 
+    /* AMIX: no DEFAULT_CHAR property means no default character, not what the
+     * caller's FontRec held (bdftopcf's is on the stack: PCFs varied run to run) */
+    pFont->info.defaultCh = (unsigned short) NO_SUCH_CHAR;
+
     if (!bdfReadProperties(file, pFont, &state))
 	goto BAILOUT;
 
